  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Cholera Response in 15 Most affected districts and populations in the country</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to reduce morbidity and mortality due to cholera in the 15 Most affected districts and populations in Zimbabwe. This WHO project provides Risk Communication and Community Engagement (RCCE), surveillance, infection prevention and control (IPC), and case management interventions in targeted high-risk districts and populations. In total, the project targets 500,000 people, including 103,054 men,111,642 women, and 285,303 children. 35,000 persons with disabilities are also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
